
Run a: cw -cp 10001 -c iod.conf common a
Run b: cw -cp 5555 -c iod.conf common b

b determines there is no channel to start and creates on, arbitrarily selets a port
b creates a command socket bound to an inproc address for external command messages
The channel adds a shadow machine and filters
Processing thread starts the channel with a command socket for processing to talk to the channel
...

Summary
Note: there is internal routing within the client (and server)

- A channel is created by sending a request to server side on the cw (command) channel
- server creates a channel and returns the name
- client connects and waits for a start message (WAITSTART)
- server sends a start
- client sets state to UPLOADING
- server sends its state
- client receives 'done' from server
- client sents ack(?)
- client received 'OK' from server and switches to DOWNLOADING
- server sends ack


